umentation\/Cycles\/UndirectedSimpleCycles","url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/undirectedsimplecycles","title":"UndirectedSimpleCycles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every simple cycle of an undirected graph once, lazily, each starting at its least vertex (in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order) and leaving it through the lesser of its two edges there: by least vertex,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and among the cycles with one least vertex in the order a depth-first search from it, taking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges in "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, meets them in that orientation."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}